    <!-- DACS 2.7 -->
    <bioghist>
      <head>Biographical/Historical Note</head>
      <p>Francis Holmes Styles was born December 15, 1895, in Lansdowne, Pennsylvania. For 32 years
        Francis Styles worked for the US Department of State and built a brilliant diplomatic
        career. He served as counsel general in Dublin, Shanghai, and Goteborg.</p>
      <p>Francis Holmes Styles is son of Samuel Styles and Mary Riley Styles, after whom the library
        in the City of Falls Church is named. </p>
      <p>In 2023, Francis Styles's daughter, Kathleen Styles, made a generous donation of letters
        and photographs to the Mary Riley Styles Public Library History Room.</p>
    </bioghist>
